FAILURES:
1. A-3 / WCAG 1.4.11 (Non-text Contrast, AA). File:
   internal/handlers/whatif/handlers.go, the new `guardrailsEnabled` trace
   block in buildProjectionChartData (~line 860, the "Raise trigger" trace
   `"color": "#22c55e"`) and the adjoining `guardrailTrace["yaxis"] = "y2"`
   reassignment (~line 970) that re-hosts the pre-existing raise-marker
   color onto the new unfilled panel. Observed: in light theme, the
   "Raise trigger" dashed line and the raise (triangle-up) markers render
   at 2.28:1 contrast against the white card background -- below the 3:1
   AA minimum for a graphical element that carries meaning (the guardrail
   raise threshold and raise events). Dark theme is fine (6.66:1). Evidence:
   gv2-audit/results.json (`light.traceContrast`, `dark.traceContrast`),
   gv2-audit/whatif-light-card.png vs whatif-dark-card.png (visual
   confirmation), independent Python WCAG-formula recomputation in this
   session's transcript. Fix direction: pick a raise-trigger/marker green
   with >=3:1 against white (e.g. a darker green such as #16a34a or
   #15803d), verified in both themes, OR give the raise elements a second
   visual weight cue (thicker stroke / larger marker) that still meets the
   graphical-contrast bar -- shape/text differentiation (A-8/A-9) is
   already fine, this is purely a contrast-value fix.
